WEBVTT

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:14.630
"Tsubasa: Tokyo Revelations"

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:22.470
<i>Where is this warmth going?</i>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:22.470
<i>Kono nukumori wa doko e yuku no</i>

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.900
<i>Come tomorrow, will it be gone?</i>

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.900
<i>Ashita ni nareba kiete shimau no</i>

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:36.200
<i>If I match the beating of my heart to yours,</i>

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:36.200
<i>Mune no kodou wo awaseta naraba</i>

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:42.620
<i>could I descend to the same depth as you?</i>

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:42.620
<i>Onaji fukami e orite yukeru no</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:49.380
<i>I'll always, always be by your side</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:49.380
<i>Itsumo itsumo soba ni iru yo</i>

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:58.220
<i>no matter how far your heart wanders</i>

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:58.220
<i>Donna tooku kimi no
kokoro ga mayotte mo</i>

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:04.730
<i>As the two of us drifted along in the darkness,</i>

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:04.730
<i>Kurayami no naka ni
futari de tadayoinagara</i>

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:11.650
<i>we brought our wings together,
like innocent little birds</i>

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:11.650
<i>Mujaki na kotori no you
ni tsubasa wo yosete ita</i>

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:18.450
<i>When you're lonely, and hide behind your smile,</i>

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:18.450
<i>Samishii toki ni wa
egao ni kakureru kimi wa</i>

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.780
<i>like an unmelting blade of ice</i>

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.780
<i>Tokenai koori no yaiba</i>

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.330
<i>you lay bare my heart</i>

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.330
<i>Kono mune wo sarashite</i>

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:30.210
<i>with your embrace</i>

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:30.210
<i>Dakishimeru</i>

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.610
The princess!

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.490
She's just sleeping.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.660
We managed to
get out of there, huh?

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.410
But Fai, I thought you weren't
going to use your magic.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.290
It was a bit different from
the magic I've used before.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.630
It's magic that uses sound,

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:21.300
which is a different variety
from the style that I learned.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.590
I'm sorry.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.560
I should have thought harder
about finding a way out of the library.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.230
Syaoran-kun, you did all that you could, right?

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.020
You got Sakura-chan's memory feather, and everything.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.150
In the land of Recolte, we were
blown away by those library watchdogs,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.190
but I have no memories after that.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.620
And yet, I still have the sensation in my feet,

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.620
like I've defeated something.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.410
What's the matter?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.420
Syaoran, does your wound hurt?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.790
I'm fine.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.340
Really?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.340
--You're so sweet, Mokona. Thanks.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.510
--You're so sweet, Mokona. Thanks.
--What is it with everyone?

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.180
Now then...

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.640
what sort of place are we in this time?

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.030
Wake up.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.410
Who's there?

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.240
Wake up.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.290
What's the deal with this place?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.550
Is something the matter?

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.170
It's these ruins.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.920
The edges of the rubble are rounded.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.800
What of it?

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.850
Even if it is weathered, I doubt
the wind alone would do this.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.060
Ouch!

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.770
This rain hurts!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.150
It burns...?

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.950
Looks like that building hasn't collapsed!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.620
Let's go!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.220
Thank goodness! It looks
like we can get out of the rain.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.690
If we'd been a little bit later,
we'd be full of holes now.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.770
We're safe!

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.810
No, not quite.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.830
I'm going to go look around inside.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.710
Be careful, okay?

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.300
Sakura-chan, it's lucky for us that you're asleep.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.180
Mokona...?

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:19.850
Mm-mm, I have to find Sakura's feather.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.900
Thanks.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.280
Can you sense a feather's presence?

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.530
I'm not sure, but I do feel a very large power.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.700
Where's it coming from?

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:31.950
Below.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.410
Mokona?

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:45.550
Syaoran!

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:49.470
If you've set foot into this place...

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.510
...you must want to die.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.520
An unfamiliar face, huh?

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.350
Those kicks were pretty cool.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.360
How can you be so casual?
He's an intruder!

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.230
And he's a thief.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.110
So, what do we do, Kamui?

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.240
Are you game?

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:17.700
"Game"?

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.470
You wander around for just a
little bit, and look what happens.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.060
Kurogane-san!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.890
White Manju bun, my katana!

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.350
Right!

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.400
You're the ones who started this.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.690
You're the leader, are you?

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.150
He sure talks big, huh?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.530
Maybe he thinks he can beat Kamui.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:55.780
That's impossible. There's only
one man who can keep up with Kamui.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.170
What's up with this guy?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.210
He uses a form I've never seen before.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.430
Kurogane!

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.480
Kurogane-san!

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.610
Shoryusen!!

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.320
Kamui!

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.450
Stay back.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:44.170
Don't you feel any pain?

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.830
He's not only strong...

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.510
...there's something different about him.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.510
Not bad. He sent Kamui flying.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:00.180
This is no time to be impressed.
We have protecting to do.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.890
You're just going to walk away?

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.860
I'll leave them to you.
The two that are hiding, as well.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.730
Where are you going?

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:12.400
Underground.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:13.900
And that's that.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:17.280
Kamui can be a handful, too.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.120
You've found us.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.370
What is there underground?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.870
Isn't that obvious?
Underground is where the water is.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.620
Water?

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.040
What do you mean?

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.750
You didn't come to get the water?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.880
We just barely got here.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:37.760
You know what? Mokona and us guys
came from a very faraway place.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.510
We don't know anything about this land.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.720
So, we're not thieves.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.680
What kind of creature is that?

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.350
Is he a mutant?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:47.650
Mokona is Mokona.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.360
He talks, as well!

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.190
Kazuki, don't approach them so lightly.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.780
Man, Nataku, you're so rough!

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.320
Well, what do we do with them, Yuto?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.490
Kamui said he would leave them to us.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:05.410
If Kamui didn't kill them, he must
have felt that it was not necessary.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:11.090
Kamui never pulls his punches when
protecting what's underground, and all.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.470
Which means there's no need
to forcibly dispose of them, huh?

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.520
That settles it. You're free to go.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.020
The only great power I can sense
around here is coming from below us.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:35.240
Well then, we can't move from
here until we investigate, can we?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.030
Um, please excuse me...

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:43.990
This boy is named Syaoran-kun.
I'm Fai, and this is Kuro-tan!

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.660
That's Kurogane!

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.870
It'd be a little rough on
him to leave him like this,

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.250
so could we trouble you for
some sort of medical attention?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.210
It would be a waste of our medicine.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:58.300
But Kamui did shoot him,
even though he wasn't a thief.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:01.930
We might not be able to offer
anything approaching "treatment,"

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.100
but come along.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.060
Kakyo...

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:07.230
If Kakyo says so, it's probably safe.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:08.480
Thanks.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.400
If you're going to stay here,
you're going to work.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.770
That's something Kuro-sama will do diligently.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.030
Don't go deciding that for me!

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.740
This will buy us a little time.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.200
Right.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.420
Sorry about this.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.710
If you feel that way, don't get beaten up.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.260
Ah, Kusanagi!

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.680
Welcome back.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.140
Hi there.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.430
It looks like someone else has come.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:46.720
It's all right.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.520
Mm-hmm, no problem.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:50.140
Are you wounded or anything?

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.400
Nope, I'm all right.

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.480
There are other people here, too.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:04.410
Wake up.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.330
Me...?

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.790
Yes. You have to wake up soon.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.710
It's been 15 years since the acid
rain has been falling like this.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:20.170
The rivers, ponds, lakes,
and other groundwater

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.680
cannot be used as drinking water.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.220
The rain has damaged the other buildings

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.390
that have filtering equipment,
so they don't work properly.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.930
What have you done for these 15 years?

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:35.020
Tokyo here has always had
an underground water vein.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:37.690
Although, it's not just the buildings.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:41.280
The ground itself is being corroded.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.990
Though it may be underground,

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.490
unless there's something covering it,

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.990
it's the same as the water on the surface.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.910
But this building doesn't look
like it's falling apart at all,

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.330
compared to the others around.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:56.460
That's why the water below
us is so precious, you know?

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.130
There's also the Tower.

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.920
Tower?

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:07.350
There's one other place that has water left.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:09.390
We're in a dispute with them.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:13.430
There's only two places,
after all, so it's no wonder.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.440
A little while ago, there
were still some other buildings

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.520
that hadn't completely fallen apart,

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.610
but right now, it's just the
Metropolitan Government Building,

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:26.910
and the Tower, that haven't
changed much over the last 15 years.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:30.830
Well then, water really is
precious in this country, huh?

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:32.200
When you say "country,"

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:37.080
only the 23 wards of Tokyo still
have any people living in them.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.840
Well, if you have to call it something,

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.670
this could be the country of Tokyo, I guess.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.340
Tokyo...

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.570
How long do I have to stay like this?

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.660
It's nice that they let us
have a place to sleep, huh?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.580
If possible, I hope you
can keep going on like this,

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:21.040
and not have to wake up in this land.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.380
Syaoran-kun could be
coming down with a fever.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:31.050
I'll stay awake and watch him,
so Kuro-sama, you get some sleep.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.520
Um, unless you answer me,

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.980
I'm going to be the questionable
man who talks to himself.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.270
Then you answer me something.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:42.730
What?

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:44.980
Why did you use magic?

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:51.070
Even in the land of Koryo,
when we were about to die,

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.330
you didn't use your magic.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:58.160
You told me then that if the
person sleeping beneath the water

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.670
in the land where you came from
woke up, he might come after you.

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:05.760
That's why you have to flee
from him, to various other worlds.

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:10.010
Kuro-rin, your memory is sharp, huh?
That's Daddy for you!

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.470
Play along.
You're leaving me hanging, you know.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.600
Whether you're being
pursued because you're a criminal,

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:21.690
or for some other reason, and
that's why you have to run away,

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.730
it makes no difference to me.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.940
That sounds like you, Kuro-sama.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.990
That is what you want, right?

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:32.160
You smile that superficial smile,
but you keep everyone at arm's length,

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.990
and won't have anything to do with others...

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:39.460
But now, you're concerned about the kid's fever,

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:43.790
and worried about the princess
learning of the misery of this land.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.960
And then there was that whistling.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:48.710
I told you, I can't die.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.760
You mean you just can't die for yourself.

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:56.930
But if you were to die for
someone else, that's another matter.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.020
If you hadn't done anything back there,

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:03.900
we would have been captured,
or worse, maybe even killed.

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.610
And yet you used your magic.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:09.650
You've involved yourself with them.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.370
I don't want to cause anyone adversity

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.040
because of their involvement with me.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.840
May we have a moment?

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:30.510
Yes! You can speak to Kuro-tan.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:33.300
Don't go thinking that
you've evaded the subject.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:35.050
You're hurting me.

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:38.350
I told you, it makes no difference to me.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:41.890
Mm-hmm, so pay no mind about me.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:46.770
Your past makes no difference. So...

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:50.110
...hurry up and resign yourself to who you are now.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.110
They're sleeping, so let's step outside.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.360
All right.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.380
That's hard for me to do.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.260
Am I...

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:18.600
...under the water?

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.690
You can't be here.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:38.570
You have to wake up, open your eyes,
before the dream takes you.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.540
Are you okay, wounded as you are?

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:47.380
Yes.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.670
If you're staying with us, you have to work.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.170
We don't have any extra food, or anything else.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.550
Okay!

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:58.590
You know, I thought that
big guy would come along.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:02.720
He wanted to come, but I asked him not to.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:06.270
Sakura-chan still hasn't woken
up, and I'm concerned about her.

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:09.060
I told him that Syaoran-kun and I wanted to go.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:10.480
Kurogane stays at home!

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:11.520
Yep!

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.360
That bastard...

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.160
The rain is letting up, huh?

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:22.950
Be on guard. They're coming out.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.620
Huh? What are?

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.340
Nice skill.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.640
I've used these in another land.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:44.850
What's that?

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.680
A mutant species.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.900
They are poisonous, but if
you avoid that, they're edible.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:53.400
Mokona was called a mutant yesterday!

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.730
Are you going to eat Mokona?

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.780
Oh, you do look tasty.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.580
Mokona! Give me my Hien!

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.040
Right!

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.470
Incredible...

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:19.010
Are you all right?

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:21.010
What about you?

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:23.720
Your leg...

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.180
I'm fine.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:33.230
You've brought down quite a big one there, huh?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.110
Who are those people?

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.980
They're from the Tower.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:43.660
What was that?

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.200
The Tower? Aren't they the
ones you're in a dispute with?

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:50.870
Yes. What's more, our own
Kamui and their leader...

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.920
You seem to be in a foul mood, Kamui.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.130
That's because I saw your face.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:19:00.260
I guess they don't get along very well, huh?

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:04.550
That's a large catch.
Food is necessary, of course,

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:09.600
but nothing is more important
than water. Right, Kamui?

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:20.610
Your movements are slower
than usual. Are you hurt?

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.660
Perhaps from his fight with Kuro-sama.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.080
He got flipped away.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.830
Pretty embarrassing, Fuma.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.710
You're right about that.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.930
Fuma, the Tower has contacted us.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:44.760
They say one of the other wards is attacking.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:48.560
If we keep messing around out here,
they'll take our water away.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.020
Oh, well.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:55.860
I think we'll be meeting again soon. See you later.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:57.570
There they go.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.320
That Fuma person is pretty strong, huh?

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:05.660
Well, here in Tokyo, he's about
the only one who can take on Kamui.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:10.080
So, have Fuma and Kamui always
been the strongest ones here?

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:15.040
No, not always. Kamui is the same as you guys.

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.880
It was about two years ago, I'd say.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.170
He suddenly showed up here in Tokyo.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:24.800
In our building. It was called the
"Metropolitan Government Building."

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:28.100
At first, we thought he was a thief, after the water.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:32.220
Back then, Kamui seemed to be a little confused.

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.430
Confused?

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:40.770
Kazuki said that Kamui was like a
child who had gotten lost back then.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:44.490
He looked at the water, and said...

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:47.110
I'm staying here.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.160
I will protect it.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.660
Protect it?

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:54.580
So then, Kamui-kun came to stay at the--

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.330
Metropolitan Government Building, was it?

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:57.750
Yeah.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:03.670
Kakyo said that you and Kamui were alike.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:08.840
She said it was because both of
you are seeking for something.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:12.310
I have to get them back, no matter what.

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.100
Mekyo!!

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.320
He has awakened.

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:53.310
Syaoran...

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:58.940
Why are you here?

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:03.480
I'm sleeping. But you have to wake up.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:07.360
I can't. I can't open my eyes.

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:13.990
Open your eyes, for the
sake of those dear to you.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:23.460
Hey! Princess! Hey!

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:29.590
She's not breathing!

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:31.180
Mekyo!!

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:33.640
The feather's presence has grown stronger!

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:36.600
Can you tell where it's coming from, Mokona?

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:39.980
Sure enough, it's under the building
where Sakura and Kurogane are.

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:41.440
Under there?

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:50.280
Fai-san!

00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:52.870
It's not water that Syaoran is after!

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:54.870
It's something that's dear to Sakura!

00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:57.330
Sakura...?

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:01.210
It's something dear to someone dear to me.

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:08.590
It looks like we couldn't
keep you sealed after all.

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:12.430
You're leaving, right? I won't block your way.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:16.680
But then, you don't have
the power to cross dimensions.

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:19.310
But I am able to.

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:21.980
I can only do it once, though.

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:30.860
Why?

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:33.740
I have to end the dream.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.370
A doctor! No, will a doctor even help?

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:43.040
It's not something that can be cured with treatment.

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:47.290
You came here from another world--
from a different dimension, right?

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:00.390
You're here.

00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:29.500
<i>All we do is search;</i>

00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:29.500
<i>Sagashite bakari no bokutachi wa</i>

00:24:29.590 --> 00:24:35.720
<i>we're so similar, it's like looking in a mirror</i>

00:24:29.590 --> 00:24:35.720
<i>kagami no you ni yoku niteru kara</i>

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:42.060
<i>We just need to face each other to connect,</i>

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:42.060
<i>mukiau dake de tsunagaru no ni</i>

00:24:42.140 --> 00:24:47.400
<i>and yet we still cannot touch</i>

00:24:42.140 --> 00:24:47.400
<i>fureau koto wa dekinai mama</i>

00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:53.570
<i>I've looked hard</i>

00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:53.570
<i>Me wo korashita</i>

00:24:53.650 --> 00:25:00.030
<i>I've reached out my hand</i>

00:24:53.650 --> 00:25:00.030
<i>Te wo nobashita</i>

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:05.750
<i>Tell me, I want to know, I want to know,</i>

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:05.750
<i>Nee boku wa, boku wa shiritai</i>

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:11.590
<i>what is it like to love?</i>

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:11.590
<i>aisuru tte donna koto?</i>

00:25:11.670 --> 00:25:24.060
<i>When you smiled, the world
shook a little and gleamed</i>

00:25:11.670 --> 00:25:24.060
<i>Kimi ga hohoemu to sekai
wa sukoshi furuete kagayaita</i>

00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:35.740
<i>It started to move, almost
as though it were breathing</i>

00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:35.740
<i>Marude kokyuu suru
you ni ugokidashita</i>

00:25:37.410 --> 00:25:43.200
<i>Tell me, I want to know, I want to know,</i>

00:25:37.410 --> 00:25:43.200
<i>Nee boku wa, boku wa shiritai</i>

00:25:43.290 --> 00:25:49.000
<i>what is it like to live?</i>

00:25:43.290 --> 00:25:49.000
<i>Ikiteku tte donna koto?</i>

00:25:49.080 --> 00:26:01.470
<i>When I asked you, the world
shook a little and gleamed</i>

00:25:49.080 --> 00:26:01.470
<i>Boku ga tazuneru to sekai
wa sukoshi furuete kagayaita</i>

00:26:01.550 --> 00:26:20.530
<i>Boku ni nemuru shinjitsu wo
ima shizuka ni tokihanatsu</i>

00:26:01.550 --> 00:26:20.530
<i>The truth that rests within
me is now quietly set free</i>
